images.caption:
The west window of Exeter Cathedral, early 20th century. Figures left to right:
King Athelstan, with below arms of Frederick Temple, Bishop of Exeter (1869-1885), Bishop of London (1885-1896) and Archbishop of Canterbury (1896-1902);
Leofric, Bishop of Exeter;
Walter de Stapledon, Bishop of Exeter 1308–1326, with above arms of See of Exeter impaling Stapledon;
King Edward the Confessor, with his attributed arms above, and the royal arms of Queen Victoria below;
Saint Peter, patron saint of Exeter Cathedral, with above arms of See of Exeter, below arms of See of Canterbury and See of York;
Queen Edyth, with attributed arms of Kingdom of Kent above;
John de Grandisson,  Bishop of Exeter 1327-1369, with above arms of See of Exeter impaling Grandison and below arms of See of Exeter impaling Temple;
Miles Coverdale, Bishop of Exeter (1551–1553), with below arms of See of London impaling Temple;
Frederick Temple, Bishop of Exeter (1869-1885), Bishop of London (1885-1896) and Archbishop of Canterbury (1896-1902), with above arms of See of Canterbury impaling Temple.

